From: FlaxAdvisors
Subject: Fix SOL activation failure when xyz.openbmc_project.Ipmi.SOL is absent

updateSOLParameter() catches std::runtime_error to handle a missing SOL
config D-Bus object, but sdbusplus exceptions (including ResourceNotFound
returned by the ObjectMapper when the object does not exist) inherit from
sdbusplus::exception_t -> std::exception, NOT std::runtime_error.

The uncaught exception propagates to the top-level handler in
sd_event_loop.cpp which logs "Executing the IPMI message failed" and
returns without sending any response.  ipmitool then times out and
reports "No response activating SOL payload".

The sol::Manager fields default to safe values (enable=true, reasonable
timings), so when the SOL config service is absent netipmid can proceed
with defaults.  Change both catch specifiers to std::exception so the
error is swallowed locally and SOL activation continues.

--- a/sol/sol_manager.cpp
+++ b/sol/sol_manager.cpp
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ void Manager::updateSOLParameter(uint8_t channelNum)
             solService = ipmi::getService(dbus, solInterface,
                                           solPathWitheEthName);
         }
-        catch (const std::runtime_error& e)
+        catch (const std::exception& e)
         {
             solService.clear();
             lg2::error("Get SOL service failed: {ERROR}", "ERROR", e);
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@ void Manager::updateSOLParameter(uint8_t channelNum)
         properties = ipmi::getAllDbusProperties(
             dbus, solService, solPathWitheEthName, solInterface);
     }
-    catch (const std::runtime_error& e)
+    catch (const std::exception& e)
     {
         lg2::error("Setting sol parameter: {ERROR}", "ERROR", e);
         return;
